From 67c77e8b2b85635ee0a78e79547ccd8d16bb3583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:30:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Export the border-fill table, and take the page from
 the section that holds the document
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A cell already carried a borderFillId but nothing could resolve it, so every HWP
table reached the host with no borders at all and was drawn with the host's own
grid — including the 423 of this file's 821 definitions that turn all four edges
off. Page geometry came from sections.first(), which in a real Korean document is
the cover: its margins made a 394-page file 458.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
